--shanling: the D-Bus service shanling.bluealsa that the Shanling Q2's own UI (demo, through Shanling's
libbtctl.so) calls and listens to, written anew in one file (src/shanling.c) from what the Q2's bluealsa 4.0.0
does on the bus, as test/bluealsa_own.py --against-stock measures it (Vamp's docs/bluealsa.md, The
compatibility service): its interface, StatusChange at a configuration and at a volume change with the same
bytes, the quality calls' numbering, and /tmp/bt_startup. Off unless asked for, so a base without the Q2's
UI leaves it out. Vamp's, not for upstream (bluez-alsa, MIT).

